\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God, what offering shall I give
\par To Thee, the Lord of earth and skies?
\par My spirit, soul, and flesh receive,
\par A holy, living sacrifice:
\par Small as it is, 'tis all my store;
\par More shouldst Thou have, if I had more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Now, O my God, Thou hast my soul,
\par No longer mine, but Thine I am;
\par Guard Thou Thine own, possess it whole,
\par Cheer it with hope, with love inflame;
\par Thou hast my spirit, there display
\par Thy glory to the perfect day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou hast my flesh, Thy hallowed shrine,
\par Devoted solely to Thy will;
\par Here let Thy light for ever shine,
\par This house still let Thy presence fill:
\par O source of life, live, dwell, and move
\par In me, till all my life be love!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Send down Thy likeness from above,
\par And let This my adorning be;
\par Clothe me with wisdom, patience, love,
\par With lowliness and purity,
\par Than gold and pearls more precious far,
\par And brighter than the morning star.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, arm me with Thy Spirit's might,
\par Since I am called by Thy great name;
\par In Thee let all my thoughts unite,
\par Of all my works be Thou the aim:
\par Thy love attend me all my days,
\par And my soul business be Thy praise.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

